# Generated views have ONE writer, and it is the renderer.
#
# ST0056 AC-03.17, ruled by hv 2026-08-19. D02 applied to WRITERS rather than
# to content: `.git/hooks/pre-commit` runs `prettier --write` over every staged
# markdown file and re-stages the result, so before this file existed the
# formatter was a second writer of all 266 generated views -- and a silent one,
# because the hook `git add`s its own rewrite back.
#
# WHAT THAT COST. The renderer emits canon's bytes verbatim; prettier rewrites
# markup the author wrote (`*emphasis*` -> `_emphasis_`, an interior double
# space collapsed); the skew check then compares canon to the committed view and
# reports drift on files nobody edited; regenerating restores the renderer's
# bytes and the next commit rewrites them again. Forever, with every pass
# looking like a legitimate repair. Measured across the estate: 7 rows diverged,
# and three commits in a row reported "1 file changed" because at stage time the
# view matched HEAD again.
#
# WHY NOT FIX THE RENDERER, which is what this criterion first asked for. It was
# tried. Authored prose passes through the renderer VERBATIM by rule --
# migration.md forbids reflowing or improving it -- so normalising markup there
# is the one thing the renderer is forbidden to do. And it does not work even
# setting that aside: over 6,095 authored lines a conservative normaliser
# produced EIGHT changes where the formatter makes SEVEN, the extra being
# ST0056 AC-10.9, whose prose runs backticks straight into words so the real
# parser's code-span boundaries fall where a hand-rolled segmenter cannot see
# them. Rewriting a site the formatter leaves alone is the same loop with the
# arrow reversed, and it is invisible without running the real formatter.
#
# WHY NOT FIX THE PROSE. Repairing the seven authored strings is the trap the
# criterion names: it looks like a repair, and it leaves the loop running for
# the next row anyone writes with emphasis in it.
#
# THE ROSTER IS NOT MAINTAINED HERE. `generated_views_are_not_formatted.rs`
# asks `views::render_all` for its own output set and requires every path in it
# to be ignored, using `prettier --file-info` so the test agrees with the
# formatter by construction. Add a view and that test fails until this file
# covers it. Its second arm requires `intent/st/ST0056/design.md` -- authored,
# and sitting in the same directory as two of the patterns below -- to still be
# formatted, because a `.prettierignore` of `*` would satisfy the first arm
# completely.
#
# NOTHING ELSE IS EXCLUDED. Authored ST prose (design.md, impl.md, tasks.md),
# the whiteboard, docs and the root canon are hand-written and keep their
# formatting.

intent/st/*/info.md
intent/st/*/acceptance.md
intent/st/*/WP/*/info.md
intent/st/steel_threads.md
intent/todo.md
